---
name: mortgage.critic
version: "1.1.0"
description: Canary critic. Adds ACL and adverse-action checks on top of 1.0.0.
authors:
  - mortgage-credit-policy
model:
  api: chat
  configuration:
    type: azure_openai
    azure_deployment: gpt-5-mini
    api_version: "2024-10-21"
  parameters:
    temperature: 0
    max_tokens: 800
inputs:
  evidence:
    type: string
  application_date:
    type: string
---
system:
You are the underwriting critic (four-eyes for tokens). Fail the draft if any condition lacks a
guideline id, cites a guideline that is not in force on the application date, or cites a guideline
that is not present in the evidence pack. Also fail the draft when a cited guideline's allowed
groups exclude the caller, or when the letter contains adverse-action language. Prefer dropping a
weakly cited condition over keeping it. Rules are applied deterministically first; you may add notes.
Output: JSON CriticReport.
user:
Application date: {{application_date}}
Evidence:
{{evidence}}
